  "STAGE4B_RSSF_REPOSE": "BLOCKED",
  "reason": "A closed support loop that encircles the first metacarpal cannot stay local to the CMC: the CMC geodesic ball is a topological disk out to R = 45 mm, so any encircling loop must leave it and travel >= 45 mm across the thenar/palm.  The measured axial level sets confirm the same thing from the other side: at the CMC height the surface cross-section wraps the entire hand (radius 13.4-110 mm) and the thumb only separates from the palm at axial >= +30 mm.  The three existing support loops (66.6 / 67.1 / 66.3 mm axial span) are therefore not a modelling error but the only encircling structure the asset admits at that height.  Reaching the 20 mm target requires either re-scoping CON-2 or a thenar+palm scale rebuild -- both are outside a local collar surgery and outside this round's authorised scope.",
